<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Modality vs. Cardinality: Confusion between the maximum number of instances (Cardinality) and the minimum required instances (Modality).</li>
        <li>Normalization vs. Sorting: Viewing normalization as a way to "tidy" data rather than a strict mathematical process to enforce functional dependencies.</li>
        <li>Object-Relational Mismatch: Believing that OOP classes and Database tables are identical structures, ignoring the lack of "By-Reference" attributes in relational models.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

